ive":"Employs approximately 268 people. Revenue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $66K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Brandywine Realty Trust is a small-cap real estate business with a $520M market cap on $484M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 15.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 543% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Brandywine Realty Trust (BDN) Stock Undervalued Right Now?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/brandywine-realty-trust-bdn-stock-134003403.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490803.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.94,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Highwoods Properties (NYSE:HIW) & Brandywine Realty Trust (NYSE:BDN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/reviewing-highwoods-properties-nysehiw-brandywine-realty-trust-nysebdn.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999714.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street's Most Accurate Analysts Spotlight On 3 Real Estate Stocks Delivering High-Dividend Yields","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/dividends/26/11/63232991/wall-streets-most-accurate-analysts-spotlight-on-3-real-estate-stocks-delivering-high-dividend-yields-11","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794570485.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"compa